der throughout the module') ,(33, 'Section numbers should not be duplicated') ,(34, 'Each section should have at least one comment line after the section name') ,(35, 'Immediately after the comment lines after the Section name at the beginning of a section there should be a start paragraph of P<section number>-START') ,(36, 'Each section should end with a P<section name>-EXIT paragraph name followed by an exit statement on the next line') ,(37, 'Each section should end with a <section name>-EXIT paragraph name followed by an exit statement on the next line e.g.') ,(38, 'All paragraph names should be prefixed  P<section number>. The suffix can be any (legal) characters') ,(39, 'A paragraph name should be on a line by itself') ,(40, 'There will be one COBOL verb per line') ,(41, 'Exit the module using GOBACK') ,(42, 'There should only be one GOBACK per module') ,(43, 'The GOBACK should be in the controlling (1st) section') ,(44, 'STOP RUN or EXIT PROGRAM should not be used') ,(45, 'Each statement should start in column 12  unless embedded within another statement') ,(46, 'An ADD statement should have a corresponding END-ADD if it is conditional') ,(47, 'A CALL statement should have a corresponding END-CALL if it is conditional') ,(48, 'A COMPUTE statement should have a corresponding END-COMPUTE if it is conditional') ,(49, 'A DELETE statement should have a corresponding END-DELETE at its end') ,(50, 'A DIVIDE statement should have a corresponding END-DIVIDE  if it is conditional') ,(51, 'An EVALUATE statement should have a corresponding END-EVALUATE at it''s end') ,(52, 'A maximum of X statements will be coded after a WHEN clause within an EVALUATE statement') ,(53, 'Indent each part of an EVALUATE statement by 3 characters') ,(54, 'Always code a ''WHEN OTHER'' clause within an EVALUATE statement') ,(55, 'The SQLCODE should not be checked following a DB2 SQL ''DECLARE CURSOR''') ,(56, 'Each DB2 SQL ''OPEN CURSOR'' should have a  corresponding DB2 SQL ''CLOSE CURSOR''') ,(57, 'GO TO statements should only go to the exit paragraph of the section that the GO TO resides in') ,(58, 'Do not use GOTO .. DEPENDING ON') ,(59, 'An IF statement should have a corresponding END-IF at its end') ,(60, 'A maximum of X levels of nested IF will be coded') ,(61, 'A maximum of X statements will be coded within an IF statement') ,(62, 'Related IF, ELSE and END-IFs should be vertically aligned') ,(63, 'The statements within an IF statement should be indented by X characters') ,(64, 'An INVOKE statement should have a corresponding END-INVOKE at its end') ,(65, 'An MULTIPLY statement should have a corresponding END-MULTIPLY if it is conditional') ,(66, 'Out-of-line PERFORMS should only perform SECTIONS (not paragraphs)') ,(67, 'Out-of-line PERFORMS should not perform a range of sections or paragraphs') ,(68, 'Indent the various parts (phrases) of a  PERFORM by X characters') ,(69, 'An in-line PERFORM statement should have a corresponding END-PERFORM at it''s end') ,(70, 'A READ statement should have a corresponding END-READ at its end') ,(71, 'The REPLACE statement should not be used') ,(72, 'A RETURN statement should have a corresponding END-RETURN at its end') ,(73, 'A REWRITE statement should have a corresponding END-REWRITE at its end') ,(74, 'A SEARCH statement should have a corresponding END-SEARCH at its end') ,(75, 'A START statement should have a corresponding END-START at its end') ,(76, 'A STRING statement should have a corresponding END-STRING at its end') ,(77, 'A SUBTRACT statement should have a corresponding END-SUBTRACT if it is conditional') ,(78, 'An UNSTRING statement should have a corresponding END-UNSTRING at its end') ,(79, 'A WRITE statement should have a corresponding END-WRITE if it is conditional') ,(80, 'An XML-GENERATE statement should have a corresponding END-XML at its end') ,(81, 'An XML-PARSE statement should have a corresponding END-XML at its end') ,(82, 'NOT is permitted only if NOT is used as a comparison operator') 